<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Canonical Event Vocabulary</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.T3" title="In Appendix C Canonical Event Vocabulary ‣ ESAA: Event Sourcing for Autonomous Agents in LLM-Based Software Engineering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents the complete event vocabulary (v0.3.0) as specified in the architecture, and <a href="#A3.T4" title="In Appendix C Canonical Event Vocabulary ‣ ESAA: Event Sourcing for Autonomous Agents in LLM-Based Software Engineering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents the simplified vocabulary observed in the <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">clinic-asr</span> case study.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Complete canonical event vocabulary (v0.3.0).</span></figcaption>
