<td id="A3.T4.6.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T4.6.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">30</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.6.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.6.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T4.6.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">phase.complete</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.6.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A3.T4.6.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.6.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.6.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">All tasks in a phase are finished.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.6.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T4.6.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">8</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The simplification from 15 to 5 event types reflects a design insight: internal orchestrator events (<span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dispatch</span>, <span id="A3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">file.write</span>, <span id="A3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">view.mutate</span>) can be inferred from the <span id="A3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">claim</span> <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">complete</span> sequence, reducing log verbosity while maintaining essential traceability guarantees. The full vocabulary remains available for environments requiring maximum granularity.</p>
</div>
</section>
